  "conclusions": [
    "With this frozen recipe, all three matched J runs have worse best validation AbsRel than L. J mean .097308 versus L .095277; paired J-L +.002031 has a descriptive scene bootstrap interval [.000322,.003623]. This is conditional on the fixed nested subset and validation scenes, not a new held-out test result.",
    "J best boundary F1 .454455 is also below L .460346; paired difference -.005891 has interval [-.011286,-.000832]. J versus R AbsRel and F1 scene intervals cross zero, while boundary-band error is lower. These outcomes do not establish that joint training can never help.",
    "All three methods improve mean overall and boundary-band errors over B0. Higher global accuracy does not imply uniform per-image or boundary detection gains; the fixed seed320112 cases contain improvements and regressions. No new image review of seeds320113/320114 is claimed.",
    "The Joint curves show decreasing training loss and different validation plateaus; seed320114 continues improving around2100-2200 and has raw best2900. This is observed generalization behavior, not proof of gradient conflict or of a particular causal mechanism.",
    "Best is selected by AbsRel. Final mean boundary F1 is R .456980, L .463915, J .447956 versus B0 .451155; J final boundary performance can degrade despite modest best-to-final AbsRel changes. Preserve both checkpoints.",
    "Only one of three L and one of three J runs meet the predefined terminal stable rule; R has zero. Stable-subset means describe these single qualifying seeds, not the entire method. None reaches the .09 target.",
    "The .10 target is confirmed at L800/300/300 and J700/1800/1000 attempted updates; R does not attain it. J shorter mean total runtime than L reflects different stopping trajectories and is not evidence of faster per-update computation or faster attainment of the common accuracy target.",
    "Raw-best steps, significant-improvement anchors and stopping steps differ: J seed320114 best2900 did not improve the2200 anchor by .2%, so patience stopped3200. This follows the frozen rule rather than stopping as soon as a new best appears.",
    "Observed means are R10.41,L24.67,J21.78 minutes; peak allocated GPU memory is approximately769/4020/4167MiB. R uses reused feature caches, whose historical shared preparation costs and incomplete end-to-end timing are separately recorded; these are not isolated hardware benchmark estimates.",
    "Only the100-label main routes are complete. Keep the same architecture/learning-rate/early-stop rules for200,400,300,500,577 and the staged S controls; do not retune to rescue these outcomes."
